              "id": "octa_tutor_010",
              "question": "What are higher-order thinking activities?",
              "answer": "These activities give your child room to think for themselves. They might compare ideas, explain a choice, solve a problem or create an answer of their own. While they practise these skills, their responses also help us get to know them better and build the personal map that informs tutor explanations.",
              "answer_status": "grounded_draft",
              "url": "https://octakidz.com/our-process",
              "score": 0.600556
            },
            {
              "id": "octa_tutor_003",
              "question": "How do my child's activity answers help the AI tutor teach them?",
              "answer": "We get to know your child through their activities. Their answers help build an evolving personal map of their likes, dislikes, subject interests and favourite stories. Our hyperpersonalised AI tutor uses this map to explain CBSE concepts in ways connected to what your child enjoys, with the aim of making learning more meaningful and concepts easier to understand.\n\nThe activities have their own value too. Each one focuses on 2–3 of our eight Natural Intelligences, giving your child practice in thinking, creating and solving problems.",
              "answer_status": "grounded_draft",
              "url": "https://octakidz.com/our-process",
              "score": 0.518418
            },
            {
              "id": "octa_tutor_016",
              "question": "How should I help my child with the activities?",
              "answer": "Give your child space to try their own ideas. You can help them understand the instructions and ask gentle questions about what they are thinking, while leaving the answer their own. Their response helps us get to know them better. If they remain stuck or you would like guidance, our team can help.",
              "answer_status": "grounded_draft",
              "url": "https://octakidz.com/our-process",
              "score": 0.528375
            },
            {
              "id": "octa_tutor_012",
              "question": "Will the AI understand everything about my child?",
              "answer": "The tutor gets to know your child better through the interests and responses reflected in their evolving personal map. This helps it choose more personal explanations, but it does not mean it understands everything about your child. Children can surprise us, discover new interests and change over time; the map should leave room for that.",
              "answer_status": "grounded_draft",
              "url": "https://octakidz.com/our-process",
              "score": 0.526004
            },
            {
              "id": "octa_tutor_006",
              "question": "What happens when my child's interests change?",
              "answer": "Children grow, and their interests grow with them. As your child completes more activities, the personal map can evolve so the tutor can draw on examples that remain relevant. A favourite story or game is a useful starting point, not a box your child has to stay in.",
              "answer_status": "grounded_draft",
              "url": "https://octakidz.com/our-process",
              "score": 0.524093
            }
